Montclair CBT
A computer-based testing (CBT) and school management portal for Montclair Group of Schools (Oke-Aro & Matogun campuses, Ogun State, Nigeria).
Students, staff and parents register from any device, the admin approves them, and everyone works from one shared database hosted by a small Node.js server.
Features
Student, staff and parent sign-up with passport photo, class, date of birth and more
Single admin account with approval workflow for new registrations
Computer-based tests (CBT) with automatic marking
Bulk question upload from Excel / CSV
Continuous assessment (CA) marks, attendance and report sheets
Notices, messages, notifications and a school gallery
Mobile-friendly interface
Tech stack
Layer	Technology
Frontend	Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript (no build step)
Backend	Node.js built-in http module — zero npm dependencies
Storage	JSON file (db.json) on the server
Excel	SheetJS loaded from the jsDelivr CDN
Requires Node.js 18 or newer.
Project structure
montclair-cbt/
├── index.html            # App entry point
├── package.json          # Root manifest (npm start runs the server)
├── vercel.json           # Optional: static hosting config for Vercel
├── assets/               # Logo, banner, gallery images, questions-template.csv
├── css/styles.css        # Styles
├── js/app.js             # Frontend application
└── server/
    ├── index.js          # Backend + static file server
    └── package.json
Run locally
bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd montclair-cbt
npm start
Open http://localhost:3001
No npm install is needed because the project has no dependencies. Set a different port with PORT=4000 npm start.
Deploy on Render
The server serves both the API and the frontend, so a single Web Service is all you need.
Important: package.json must be at the root of your repository. If you zip or upload the project, make sure you push the contents of the montclair-cbt folder, not the folder itself.
1. Create the service
Push the project to GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket.
In the Render dashboard, choose New → Web Service and connect the repository.
2. Use these settings
Setting	Value
Language	Node
Root Directory	(leave blank)
Build Command	npm install
Start Command	npm start
Health Check Path	/api/health
Instance Type	Free (or any paid tier)
Render automatically provides the PORT variable and the server reads it, so there is nothing to configure for networking.
3. Optional environment variables
Variable	Purpose	Default
PORT	Port the server listens on (set by Render)	3001
DATA_DIR	Folder where db.json is stored	server/data
NODE_VERSION	Pin the Node.js version, for example 20	Render default
4. Keep your data safe (persistent disk)
Render's free instances have an ephemeral filesystem: the database is wiped on every redeploy or restart. To keep data permanently:
Upgrade the service to a paid instance type.
Add a Disk under the service's Disks tab with mount path /var/data.
Add the environment variable DATA_DIR=/var/data.
Free-tier services also sleep after a period of inactivity, so the first request after a break can take about a minute.
Uploading questions in bulk
Upload a .csv or Excel file from the admin / staff question page. The first row must be:
question,optionA,optionB,optionC,optionD,correct,marks
correct can be the full answer text or the letter A, B, C or D
marks is the score awarded for the question
A sample file is included at assets/questions-template.csv
Security notes
There is exactly one admin account. Nobody else can register as admin.
Passwords are stored as SHA-256 hashes, never in plain text.
Do not publish admin credentials or the school registration code in this README or in a public repository. Share them privately with the people who need them.
Back up db.json regularly, especially before redeploying.
Troubleshooting
Problem	Fix
Render: "Could not find package.json"	The repo root is wrong. Push the contents of montclair-cbt, not its parent folder.
Render: "Port scan timeout / no open ports"	Use Start Command npm start and do not hard-code a port.
Data disappears after redeploy	You are on the free tier. Attach a disk and set DATA_DIR (see above).
Users on different phones see different data	The app is being opened as static files. Use the Render URL, not a local index.html.
Excel upload does nothing	Check your internet connection (SheetJS loads from a CDN) and the column headers.
